<title>USA: NY business loans rose $901 mln in Oct 23 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans rose $901 mln in Oct 23 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $901 million to $42,175 million in the week ended Oct 23, said Federal Reserve Bank of New York.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $906 million to $42,425 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $105 million to $755,758 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
